{
  "title": "Rectus Femoris Strain",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3104/rectus-femoris-strain",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 1 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A rectus femoris strain is a traumatic injury caused by overstretching of the muscle which results in tearing of the muscle fibers of the rectus femoris.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with tenderness over the rectus femoris made worse with resisted hip flexion or extension.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is conservative with NSAIDs, rest and stretching.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "seen more commonly in soccer and football players",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "sudden, forceful eccentric contraction of the muscle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "sprinting from standing position",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "kicking soccer ball with great force",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "acute injuries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "usually more distal on the thigh",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "chronic injuries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "usually occur closer to the muscle origin",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**avulsion of anterior inferior iliac spine** (AIIS)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "adolescent athletes may have proximal bony avulsion of anterior inferior iliac spine (AIIS)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "occurs at insertion site of direct head of rectus femoris",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
